## Why This Is Asked

Assess ability to design production-grade, multilingual, real-time NLP with auditability and privacy in a global setting.

## Key Concepts

- Real-time streaming architecture with on-device first-pass
- Retrieval-augmented detection that cites policy clauses
- Privacy-preserving inference (DP/federated) and data provenance
- Drift monitoring, versioned policies, staged rollout

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example integration stub for policy retrieval
async function flagPost(post, policyIndex) {
  const clause = await fetchPolicyClause(policyIndex, post.language);
  const isFlag = await detector.score(post, policyIndex);
  return isFlag ? {postId: post.id, clause} : null;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you evaluate and mitigate false positives across languages during policy updates?
- How do you design the provenance log and audits to satisfy regulatory requirements?

## Why This Is Asked
Addresses real-time multilingual safety, reduces model hallucinations, and tight latency with on-device processing and privacy-preserving checks.

## Key Concepts
- Retrieval-Augmented Generation
- On-device inference
- External verifier for factuality
- Drift detection and explainability
- Auditable rollback

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-pipeline wiring
const stream = createLiveStream(source);
stream.map(msg => translateToEN(msg)).then(en => {
  const intent = classifyIntent(en);
  const knowledge = fetchKB(en, intent);
  const reply = generatePolicyResponse(knowledge, en);
  if (verifyWithSources(reply, knowledge)) emit(reply);
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you keep the private KB synchronized with policy updates without downtime?
- How would you quantify and meet the <180 ms latency target under load?

