## Why This Is Asked
This question probes real-time multilingual NLP design with privacy, per-tenant isolation, and governance. It tests architecture, data flow, error handling, and testing strategies for production-grade latency.

## Key Concepts
- Real-time multilingual inference
- Per-tenant privacy-preserving embeddings
- Unified normalization taxonomy
- Edge-first deployment and latency guarantees
- Drift detection and governance annotation loop

## Code Example
```javascript
// DP-encoder sketch (conceptual)
function dpEncode(text, epsilon) {
  // apply noise to embedding vector
  const vec = embed(text);
  return vec.map(v => v + laplace(0, 1/epsilon));
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate drift between tenants without leaking data?
- What rollback strategy would you implement if a taxonomy update causes misclassification?

